+# Pickup reminders
+
+For volunteers changing pickup reminders or proposing email to save the SMS cost. Pickup reminders use SMS because
+the April–June 2025 email trial coincided with more missed pickups and wasted fresh food. Volunteers have repeatedly
+proposed email since then; this page preserves why SMS was kept.
+
+## Why SMS
+
+The [discussion in issue 52](../../notes/issue-52.md) records the trial and the decision to keep SMS. Email was free,
+while SMS cost 40 euros a month. During the April–June 2025 email trial, the provider reported that 34% of reminder
+emails were never opened. Missed pickups rose from 6% to 13% of pantry orders. Each missed pickup left a packed bag,
+whose fresh food went in the bin by closing time.
+
+The pantry lead reported that many members share one phone within the family and never check email, but see SMS.
+The team switched back to SMS on July 1, and missed pickups were back to 6% by August.
+
+SMS's recurring cost is accepted to reach members and reduce missed pickups and food waste. Free email did not
+provide an adequate replacement in the trial; its sending cost alone does not account for those consequences.
+
+## Implementation
+
+The [reminder code](../../larder/reminders.py) owns the sending behavior and timing.
